        <div class='pricerow'><div><b>{{ cwg_price }}</b><small>One payment. Instant PDF download.</small></div><a class='btn' href='{{ book_url }}'>See inside the book</a></div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class='uses' aria-labelledby='aih-uses'>
  <div class='wrap'>
    <div class='uses-head'>
      <div>
        <span class='eyebrow'>What you'll be able to do</span>
        <h2 class='h2' id='aih-uses'>Real work, handed to AI, checked by you.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class='sub' style='max-width:40ch'>Each skill has its own chapter, worked through on a real example with files you can open.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class='use-grid'>
      <li class='card' data-rv><figure><img src='{{ 'aisa-use-research.jpg' | file_img_url: '800x' }}' srcset='{{ 'aisa-use-research.jpg' | file_img_url: '600x' }} 600w, {{ 'aisa-use-research.jpg' | file_img_url: '1000x' }} 1000w' sizes='(max-width: 600px) 100vw, (max-width: 1080px) 50vw, 300px' width='1400' height='1045' alt='Highlighting a printed source' loading='lazy'></figure><div class='card-body'><span class='tag'>CH. 13–14</span><h3>Research you can cite</h3><p>Turn a real question into a sourced report, and check every citation before you rely on it.</p></div></li>
      <li class='card' data-rv><figure><img src='{{ 'aisa-use-data.jpg' | file_img_url: '800x' }}' srcset='{{ 'aisa-use-data.jpg' | file_img_url: '600x' }} 600w, {{ 'aisa-use-data.jpg' | file_img_url: '1000x' }} 1000w' sizes='(max-width: 600px) 100vw, (max-width: 1080px) 50vw, 300px' width='1400' height='1045' alt='Charts on a laptop' loading='lazy'></figure><div class='card-body'><span class='tag'>CH. 16</span><h3>Data you can prove</h3><p>Clean and analyze spreadsheets with figures computed by code, not guessed.</p></div></li>
      <li class='card' data-rv><figure><img src='{{ 'aisa-use-documents.jpg' | file_img_url: '800x' }}' srcset='{{ 'aisa-use-documents.jpg' | file_img_url: '600x' }} 600w, {{ 'aisa-use-documents.jpg' | file_img_url: '1000x' }} 1000w' sizes='(max-width: 600px) 100vw, (max-width: 1080px) 50vw, 300px' width='1400' height='1045' alt='A printed report with charts' loading='lazy'></figure><div class='card-body'><span class='tag'>CH. 15, 19</span><h3>Documents and decks</h3><p>Reports, slide decks, one-pagers, and dashboards that live beyond the chat.</p></div></li>
      <li class='card' data-rv><figure><img src='{{ 'aisa-use-automation.jpg' | file_img_url: '800x' }}' srcset='{{ 'aisa-use-automation.jpg' | file_img_url: '600x' }} 600w, {{ 'aisa-use-automation.jpg' | file_img_url: '1000x' }} 1000w' sizes='(max-width: 600px) 100vw, (max-width: 1080px) 50vw, 300px' width='1400' height='1045' alt='A calm desk with a clock at golden hour' loading='lazy'></figure><div class='card-body'><span class='tag'>CH. 27–28</span><h3>Work that runs itself</h3><p>Connect your apps, write reusable skills, and schedule tasks that run on time without you.</p></div></li>
    </ul>
    <div class='more' data-rv><span>Also inside:</span><b>Tools without coding</b><b>Claude Code and the API</b><b>Business and career</b><b>Content systems</b><b>Learning and languages</b></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class='why' aria-labelledby='aih-why'>
  <div class='wrap'>
    <span class='eyebrow'>Why now</span>
    <h2 class='h2' id='aih-why'>Why learning AI now matters more than ever.</h2>
    <p class='sub'>Work is changing faster than most training can keep up with. The people who learn to hand AI real work, and check what comes back, are the ones who move ahead.</p>
    <div class='why-grid'>
      <div class='stat' data-rv>
        <b>39%</b>
        <p>of workers' core skills are expected to change by 2030, and AI and big data top the list of fastest-growing skills.</p>
        <span class='src'>World Economic Forum, Future of Jobs Report 2025</span>
      </div>
      <ul class='points'>
        <li data-rv><i>01</i><h3>It's a skill, not a talent</h3><p>Getting reliable work out of AI is a method you can learn: how to brief it, how to check it, and how to test it.</p></li>
        <li data-rv><i>02</i><h3>The gap compounds</h3><p>Every month you hand AI more of your work, the next task gets faster. Starting later means catching up longer.</p></li>
        <li data-rv><i>03</i><h3>Trust is the real edge</h3><p>Anyone can get an answer. Knowing which answers to trust, and proving it, is what clients and managers pay for.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

